==Background==
[[File:A graffito in honour of Jose Mourinho in the streets of Rome.jpg|thumb|A graffito in honour of Jose Mourinho in the streets of Rome]]
This was Roma's third final in a major UEFA competition, having lost the [[1984 European Cup final]] to [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]] and the [[1991 UEFA Cup final]] to fellow Italian club [[Inter Milan]], who were the most recent Italian club to reach a European final – losing in the [[2020 UEFA Europa League final]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaconferenceleague/match/2033448--roma-vs-leicester/|title=Roma-Leicester |website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=5 May 2022|access-date=5 May 2022}}</ref> Roma was seeking to win their first trophy since the [[2007–08 Coppa Italia]], and a first European title for an Italian side since Inter won the [[2010 UEFA Champions League final]]. Their head coach [[José Mourinho]], having become the first manager to reach European finals with four different clubs – including the aforementioned 2010 Champions League final, was seeking to become only the third manager – after [[Udo Lattek]] and [[Giovanni Trapattoni]] – to have [[UEFA club competition records and statistics#List of managers to have won the three main European club competitions|won all three existing major European trophies]], and the first to achieve the UEFA treble by winning the [[UEFA Champions League|European Champion Clubs' Cup/UEFA Champions League]], [[UEFA Europa League|UEFA Cup/Europa League]], and UEFA Europa Conference League (in place of the now-defunct [[UEFA Cup Winners' Cup]]).<ref name="ROMFEY"/>

This was Feyenoord's fourth final in a major UEFA competition, having won the [[1970 European Cup final]] and both the [[1974 UEFA Cup final|1974]] and [[2002 UEFA Cup final|2002]] UEFA Cup finals. The first Dutch club to reach a European final since [[De Klassieker|their rivals]] [[AFC Ajax|Ajax]] lost the [[2017 UEFA Europa League final]] to Mourinho's [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]] and the most recent to win a European title, they were seeking to join [[Juventus FC|Juventus]], Ajax, [[FC Bayern Munich|Bayern Munich]], [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] and Manchester United as the only clubs to have [[UEFA club competition records and statistics#List of teams to have won the main European club competitions|won all three existing major European trophies]], and the first to achieve the UEFA treble by winning the European Champion Clubs' Cup/UEFA Champions League, UEFA Cup/Europa League and UEFA Europa Conference League (again in place of the Cup Winners' Cup). Their head coach [[Arne Slot]] was seeking to become the first Dutch to win a European trophy since [[Dick Advocaat]] with [[FC Zenit Saint Petersburg|Zenit Saint Petersburg]] in the [[2008 UEFA Super Cup]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaconferenceleague/match/2033449--marseille-vs-feyenoord/|title=Marseille-Feyenoord |website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=5 May 2022}}</ref><ref name="ROMFEY">{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaconferenceleague/news/0272-148692fa0a08-b95ab7bc5187-1000--final-roma-vs-feyenoord/|title=UEFA Europa Conference League final: Roma vs Feyenoord|website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220505223803/https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaconferenceleague/news/0272-148692fa0a08-b95ab7bc5187-1000--final-roma-vs-feyenoord/|archive-date=5 May 2022 |date=5 May 2022}}</ref>

The two sides previously met twice in European competitions, in the [[2014–15 UEFA Europa League]] [[2014–15 UEFA Europa League knockout phase#Round of 32|round of 32]], with Roma won one and drew one.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaconferenceleague/news/0272-145984bdbe35-d22360e0966d-1000--uefa-europa-conference-league-final-head-to-head-records/|title=UEFA Europa Conference League: Final head-to-head records|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220506021420/https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaconferenceleague/news/0272-145984bdbe35-d22360e0966d-1000--uefa-europa-conference-league-final-head-to-head-records/|website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=5 May 2022|archive-date=6 May 2022}}</ref>

