==Pre-match==

===Identity===
The logo of the 2022 UEFA Europa Conference League Final was unveiled at the group stage draw on 27 August 2021 in [[Istanbul]].{{citation needed|date=October 2022}}

===Ambassador===
The ambassador for the final was former Albanian international [[Lorik Cana]].{{citation needed|date=October 2022}}

===Officials===
[[File:István Kovács referee.jpg|thumb|upright=.7|Romanian referee [[István Kovács (referee)|István Kovács]] officiated the final.]]

On 11 May 2022, UEFA announced Romanian [[István Kovács (referee)|István Kovács]], a [[FIFA International Referees List|FIFA referee]] since 2010, would officiate the final. Kovács officiated six matches in the [[2021–22 UEFA Champions League|2021–22 Champions League]], three matches in the [[2021–22 UEFA Europa League|2021–22 Europa League]] and one group stage fixture in the 2021–22 Europa Conference League season. He served as a referee at [[UEFA Euro 2020]], where he officiated one group stage match. He also was a referee at the [[2014 UEFA European Under-19 Championship]], [[2019 UEFA European Under-21 Championship]] and [[2019 FIFA U-17 World Cup]]. He was joined by his fellow countrymen Vasile Marinescu and Ovidiu Artene as assistant referees. [[Sandro Schärer]] of Switzerland served as the fourth official, while German [[Marco Fritz]] was appointed as the video assistant referee. Fritz's compatriots [[Christian Dingert]] and [[Bastian Dankert]] served as the assistant and support VAR officials, respectively.<ref name="officials"/>

